invariant: INV-46
file: src/mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: a host object's mlk_noise squeezes the PRF stream and then runs
  mlk_sample_cbd, which squeezes it again and writes the same noise with
  gcc's loop of shifts by a register. Every comparison passes, because the
  coefficients are the same, so the script compiles mlkem.c for each host
  target and requires it to call mlk_vector_noise and not mlk_sample_cbd
  (docs/decisions.md 225).

--- old
    mlk_vector_noise(p, stream);
--- new
    mlk_sample_cbd(p, seed, nonce);
